Data source (web parity):
  useChargingSessionsPaginated(vehicleId, { limit: 2000, start, end }) -> GET /charging
  The web fires one paginated sessions query; the Apple seam is
  ChargingHeatmapDataSource.loadSessions(vehicleID:range:) -> [ChargingHeatmapSession],
  bound through ChargingHeatmapPageModel (no networking in the view, ADR-004). The header
  RangePicker maps to the ChargingHeatmapRange preset enum (web DEFAULT_PRESET_IDS:
  today/7d/30d/mtd/ytd/all, default 'all') driving the query's start/end window.
SI discipline (ADR-005): sessions carry SI watt-hours (total_energy_added_wh) and ISO
  timestamps; durations are derived in SI seconds. The page's two fixed display units —
  kWh (web hard-codes convertEnergyFromSI(_, 'kWh')) and minutes (web durationMinutes) —
  are produced ONLY at the SwiftUI render boundary via the shared Units facade
  (Units.convertEnergy / Units.convertDuration with kWh/min-forced UnitPreferences). Nothing
  non-SI is stored or computed; cost is a plain decimal (web Currency).

